first_10_rows.Long Description:
**Requirements:**
• Experience with PHP 2+ years;
• Strong knowledge and work experience with Laravel;
• Experience with JavaScript (Vue.js);
• Excellent knowledge of databases (MySQL);
• Experience working with GIT;
• Good problem-solving abilities;
• English - Intermediate.

**Will be plus:**
• Server management.

**We offer:**
• Friendly teams, experienced colleagues, and perfect work equipment;
• Opportunities for career growth and raising professional skills;
• Competitive compensation and regular results-based salary review;
• Your bookkeeping will be maintained by a professional accountant;
• 21 paid vacation days;
• Flexible work schedules;
• Comfortable office in the city center;
• Compensation of English courses.

**Responsibilities**:
• Develop new user-facing features;
• Translate designs and wireframes into high quality code;
• Join forces with product and design teams to define, iterate and implement new features;
• Maintain the existing project in the same stack.

**Requirements:**
- 2+ years of experience and proven track records in sales;
- Excellent communication skills (both verbal and written);
- Advanced level of English;
- Software development process understanding and IT industry knowledge;
- Good understanding of the US and European markets and ability to manage operations there.

**What to do:**
- Opportunities qualification;
- Customer negotiations, proposals development and closing;
- Creation of customized messages;
- Creation of sales presentations;
- Cooperation with the sales team (leadgen, pre-sales, marketing) ;
- Collaboration with delivery experts during the sales process;
- RFIs/RFPs Management;
- Achieving growth and hitting sales quota;
- Management and maintenance of opportunities in CRM;
- Build and evolve strong customer relationships by nurturing them and understanding their needs;
- Identifying new sales opportunities.

**What we offer:**
- Work with english-speaking customers in well organized agile environment;
- Participating in decision-making and business management processes;
- Minimal bureaucracy and proximate contact with CEO and CTO;
- Build your own work schedule without a need to be in the office all day long and owertimes.

**About You**
- In this role, you should be able to work independently with little supervision;
- You should have excellent organization and problem-solving skills;
- You have an eye for the details.
